Subject: [PATCH] r4.1 exit footsteps: outdoor steps 10-12 dB under
 music+ambience (recording-calibrated), indoor unchanged
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

运镜bot's cfe6429 recording (Chromium web build, master tap): outdoor steps sat 10-20 dB under the bed
(400 ms K-weighted momentary), late grass/path barely audible as the wind bed rises.

- STEP_GAIN: stone 0.38 -> 0.50 (+2.4 dB), path 0.34 -> 0.36 (+0.5), grass 0.32 -> 0.36 (+1.0); wood/rug unchanged.
- STEP_WIND_LIFT outdoors: +6 dB x smoothstep(0.3, 0.9, wind) (WorldFlow.getWindStrength, same source as the walk
  driver), <= 1.5 dB per 0.1 wind, so steps follow the wind bed without a jump.
- STEP_VARIANT_TRIM_DB outdoors level-matches the 4 files per surface (path_1 was 3.1 dB under path_2);
  outdoor jitter +-1.5 -> +-0.75 dB, so neighbours stay within ~3 dB. Indoor: gain, jitter, files exactly as cfe6429.
- Recording re-scaled with the new volumes: outdoor 13.1 dB (6.4..19.6) -> 11.4 dB under (median 11.0);
  door wood->stone +1.7 dB (exit), stone->wood -1.7 dB (return); outdoor neighbour max +1.3 dB.
- Low-pass, assets, timing (STEP_LEAD_S, plants) untouched.
- tools/exit-footsteps/recording_levels.py: per-step step/bed loudness from a master-tap recording (read-only).
- test_footsteps: levels locked (indoor = cfe6429, outdoor gains/trims/lift), neighbour/door test on the real
  exit + return, wind wiring; mix_preview uses the new levels.
